# Nudged positions: position_nudge

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:giggly, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
  ])
```

## About this notebook

This notebook follows the examples on ggplot2's reference page for
[`position_nudge()`](https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/position_nudge.html), in the order
the page gives them. Each example shows ggplot2's code first and then Giggly's. An example Giggly
cannot draw yet keeps its ggplot2 code and names what it is waiting for, so the page is also a
list of what remains.

`position_nudge()` moves every item a fixed distance along `x`, `y` or both, which is most useful
for shifting items on a discrete scale by a small amount. Labels are the usual case, so
`geom_text()` builds it in, as its `nudge_x` and `nudge_y` options; the distances can also be
mapped, as the `nudge_x` and `nudge_y` aesthetics, to move each item its own way. Giggly has none
of it yet, nor `geom_text()`.

## Labels on the points

```r
df <- data.frame(
  x = c(1,3,2,5),
  y = c("a","c","d","c")
)

ggplot(df, aes(x, y)) +
  geom_point() +
  geom_text(aes(label = y))
```

Unnudged, each label is drawn over its point.

Not in Giggly yet: `geom_text()` and mapping `label`.

## Nudging the labels down

```r
ggplot(df, aes(x, y)) +
  geom_point() +
  geom_text(aes(label = y), position = position_nudge(y = -0.1))
```

Not in Giggly yet: `geom_text()`, mapping `label`, and `position_nudge()`.

## Nudging in brief

```r
# Or, in brief
ggplot(df, aes(x, y)) +
  geom_point() +
  geom_text(aes(label = y), nudge_y = -0.1)
```

Not in Giggly yet: `geom_text()` and its `nudge_y` option, and mapping `label`.

## Nudging each label its own way

```r
# For each text individually
ggplot(df, aes(x, y)) +
  geom_point() +
  geom_text(aes(label = y, nudge_y = c(-0.1, 0.1, -0.1, 0.1)))
```

A vector in `aes()` gives one value per row, so the labels go down and up in turn.

Not in Giggly yet: `geom_text()`, mapping `label` and `nudge_y`, and an expression in a mapping,
such as `c(-0.1, 0.1, -0.1, 0.1)`.
